      "statement": "The Kanban UI shows four actor columns (Human, Todo, Running, Done) but each card carries a finer 13-stage classification (triage, interview, spec_approval, awaiting_merge, blocked, grill, spec_draft, spec_audit, building, review, recovery, packaging, done; HUMAN_STAGES = the five Human-column stages); resolve_status_assignee deterministically derives the canonical assignee for a target status and derive_task_stage computes the stage from status + assignee + pr_url + metadata.",
