    {
      "id": "claim_e556e1f4f4ad45b9a40fac70392d394e",
      "statement": "Every task status change funnels through one primitive, transition_task: it validates the transition against the VALID_TRANSITIONS graph (done only transitions back to triage; non-human agents are rejected from edges outside the graph with InvalidStateTransitionError), then runs a two-phase commit — Phase 1 tears down OS resources outside the DB transaction (terminate old worker, clear process artifacts) and Phase 2 atomically updates status, assignee, worker_pid, started_at, blocked_reason, and metadata, clearing stale failure/triage counters as the target state requires, then logs a task_activity row.",
